%S A400087 2,2,1,2,6,3,1,0,9,9,7,2,7,2,4,0,8,8,3,6,1,4,5,2,6,3,8,5,0,3,6,6,8,6,
%T A400087 0,1,5,5,9,9,4,0,3,2,7,1,4,5,6,2,3,3,8,8,7,3,9,2,0,9,0,5,8,5,3,6,2,6,
%U A400087 8,0,5,5,1,0,7,7,9,3,6,2,4,0,9,8,1,3,4
%N A400087 Decimal expansion of the volume of the convex hull of the ten-charge Thomson configuration on the unit sphere.
%C A400087 The configuration is a gyroelongated square dipyramid with one vertex at each pole and two square rings at heights h and -h, rotated by Pi/4 relative to each other. Graham reports its Coulomb-energy optimality in the linked preprint.
%H A400087 Peter Graham, <a href="https://hexagonmath.org/2611.00836v1">The Thomson problem for N = 10</a>, 2026.
%H A400087 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GyroelongatedSquareDipyramid.html">Gyroelongated Square Dipyramid</a>.
%H A400087 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ThomsonProblem.html">Thomson Problem</a>.
%F A400087 V = (4/3)*(1-h^2)*(1+(1+sqrt(2))*h), where h is the positive ring height.
%t A400087 Module[{x, e, h}, e = (4 Sqrt[2] + 2)/Sqrt[1 - x^2] + Sum[8/Sqrt[2 + 2 s x] + 8/Sqrt[2 + 2 x^2 + s Sqrt[2] (1 - x^2)], {s, {-1, 1}}];
%t A400087 	h = x /. FindRoot[Evaluate[D[e, x] == 0], {x, 423/1000}, WorkingPrecision -> 120, PrecisionGoal -> 100];
%t A400087 	First[RealDigits[4/3 (1 - h^2) (1 + (1 + Sqrt[2]) h), 10, 87]]] (* _Eric W. Weisstein_, Nov 24 2026 *)
%Y A400087 Cf. A400086 (positive ring height).
%Y A400087 Cf. A339262 (maximum volume of an inscribed ten-vertex polyhedron).
%K A400087 nonn,cons,new
%O A400087 1,1
%A A400087 _Eric W. Weisstein_, Nov 24 2026
